    description: "Per WI-tolif scope-expansion (Structural Fix Protocol). The 2026-04-23 audit moved Python sys.stdout/sys.stderr from ipc_send to logging. Same pattern lives in:\n- c.yaml line 85: stdout, stderr under ipc_send\n- javascript.yaml line 215: console (stdout, stderr) under ipc_send\n- rust.yaml lines 132-133: io::stdout / io::stderr functions\n- scala.yaml line 131: stdout / stdoutUtf8 / stderrUtf8 (in fs_write currently — different bucket but same threat-modeling distinction worth verifying)\n- elixir.yaml: IO.puts and friends (already labeled but verify boundary)\n- haskell.yaml: handle-based stderr writes\n\nFor each, the test pattern is the same as the Python case (test_python_catalog_stdio_is_logging_not_ipc_send): assert lookup_with_module returns boundary == 'logging'. Move the entries from ipc_send (or wherever they are) to a new 'logging' block in the YAML. stdio reads (stdin) stay in ipc_recv — they CAN carry untrusted piped input.\n\nAcceptance: 'hypergumbo io-boundaries' on a hypergumbo-style repo in each of these languages shows ipc_send chain count drop and a corresponding logging bucket appear. Tag awaits_bakeoff_validation if shipping under that policy."  # 4424
    fields: {}  # 4424
